# Cloudflare Pages headers.
# HTML must never be reused from cache/bfcache so a soft refresh always
# fetches the index.html that references the latest hashed JS bundle (a stale
# bundle points at the old *.workers.dev API, which Brave/blockers block).
#
# Cloudflare Pages COMBINES (does not override) Cache-Control across matching
# rules, so a scoped /assets/* immutable rule would merge with the /* rule
# into a contradictory "no-store, immutable" header. We therefore keep one
# unambiguous global rule. Hashed asset filenames change per build, so
# no-store is safe (just not maximally cache-efficient); revisit later if
# repeat-load performance ever matters.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
